# GitHub language statistics (Linguist) only — this file changes nothing about
# how the code builds or runs.
#
# The web client is first-party code and stays in the repo. Excluding it from
# language detection keeps the repo-page language bar reflecting the backend,
# where the substantive engineering lives (FastAPI, Postgres, the ingest
# pipeline). `-linguist-detectable` rather than `linguist-vendored` because
# "vendored" means third-party code checked in, which this is not.
frontend/** -linguist-detectable

